# Alpha Release Report

Schema: `mpk.alpha_release_report.v0`

Milestone: `ALPHA-007`

Scope: apply `develop/roadmap/RELEASE_GATES.md` to the current alpha artifacts
and release evidence. This report uses `release-report.json` from CI-008 and
the local alpha demo guide in `docs/alpha-demo.md`.

## Summary

ALPHA-007 is reproducible locally with the commands listed below.

Gate result:

| Gate | Status | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A: Trust boundary | Pass | Checkers accept only canonical certificate bytes or checked theory certificates; `docs/alpha-demo.md` documents GIR/VC artifacts as non-proof helper artifacts. |
| B: Canonicality | Pass | `./scripts/check-all.sh` exercises canonical decode/re-encode, non-canonical rejection fixtures, and hash recomputation. |
| C: Determinism | Pass | `./scripts/check-all.sh` and `scripts/generate-release-report.py --check` reproduce stable hashes, reports, and deterministic rejection fixtures. |
| D: Checker agreement | Pass | Rust source-free checker and Go reference checker agree through `scripts/check-reference.sh` and `mpk package verify-certs`. |
| E: Axiom | Pass | `release-report.json` records zero total axioms and zero external axioms for the package certificate. |
| F: Go frontend | Pass | Go version, Go source hashes, `go2gir` binary hash, GIR hashes, and VC hashes are recorded below. |
| G: Performance | Pass with documented limit | The full local suite and 10,000 invalid-candidate benchmark pass. No numeric release budget threshold is defined in `RELEASE_GATES.md`; ALPHA-004 records the current local timing profile. |
| H: Security | Pass with documented exception | Rust checker-facing crates forbid unsafe code and the Go checker source does not import `unsafe`; `go list -deps` still includes Go's standard `unsafe` package through the standard library dependency closure. |

Strict release note: Gate G and Gate H have documented limits/exceptions. A
release process that requires unqualified gate success should either approve the
documented exceptions or refine the gate checks before tagging a release.

